# #1974 (P21a): a statement-scoped `@suppress(...)` decorates a `let` exactly as it decorates a
# keywordless store — the decorated `let` parses (the decorator reaches ParseSimpleStatement) and
# runs. Whether SPY0451 is then actually suppressed is the same for `let` and for a bare
# `unused = 1` (at base 05824d52f it is NOT suppressed for either — findings ledger), so no
# .warning sidecar pins it here.
def main():
    @suppress(SPY0451)
    let unused = 1
    print("ok")
